WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.627
- Hi everybody. Oh, a live audience.

00:00:02.627 --> 00:00:04.650
- Have y'all met? Have you met Constance?

00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:06.990
- We have met, you've
been over on our show

00:00:06.990 --> 00:00:08.400
and of course on red carpets

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:10.110
and it's so good to see you again.

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:11.130
- Yeah, it's good to see you too.

00:00:11.130 --> 00:00:12.540
- And I'm excited about your memoir.

00:00:12.540 --> 00:00:13.373
- Thank you.

00:00:13.373 --> 00:00:15.907
- Okay so Kit, you say
there was one week that-

00:00:15.907 --> 00:00:17.730
of your life that really challenged you.

00:00:17.730 --> 00:00:18.563
What was that like, 'cause-

00:00:18.563 --> 00:00:19.740
- Well, any parent-

00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:22.011
every week has been challenging.

00:00:22.011 --> 00:00:24.360
But no, I was listening to you backstage

00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:25.890
and of course you and I
talked last time we were on

00:00:25.890 --> 00:00:27.420
everything that you've been through.

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:29.310
I think everybody goes
through so much stuff.

00:00:29.310 --> 00:00:31.260
You never know what's going on
in someone else's life and...

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:32.093
- [Kelly] Amen.

00:00:32.093 --> 00:00:32.926
- Your producers were asking me that.

00:00:32.926 --> 00:00:33.759
I thought about it.

00:00:33.759 --> 00:00:36.510
I had this one week where
my house had burned down.

00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:37.350
I lost everything I own

00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:39.000
when I was eight months
pregnant with my third child.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:40.597
Everything, pictures, everything.

00:00:40.597 --> 00:00:41.717
- [Constance] Oh my God.

00:00:41.717 --> 00:00:42.690
- I was removed from my job.

00:00:42.690 --> 00:00:45.090
They decided to go in a
different direction at ESPN.

00:00:45.090 --> 00:00:47.190
So I was sort of let go,
which never feels good

00:00:47.190 --> 00:00:49.110
but it was the right move for ESPN.

00:00:49.110 --> 00:00:51.450
My parents got divorced
after 40 years of marriage

00:00:51.450 --> 00:00:53.370
and my cousin took his own life.

00:00:53.370 --> 00:00:56.160
It was like it a little more
than a week, a couple of weeks.

00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:59.216
But I had that moment where
I was like, okay this is...

00:00:59.216 --> 00:01:00.135
- How much can one handle.

00:01:00.135 --> 00:01:03.240
- One handle. But you never
know what someone's going

00:01:03.240 --> 00:01:04.320
through in their life.

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:06.630
And I was born on third
base having the mom

00:01:06.630 --> 00:01:08.250
and dad and brother that I have that

00:01:08.250 --> 00:01:11.790
with that support and love
and I am rose colored glasses.

00:01:11.790 --> 00:01:12.840
Like for example...

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:13.673
- You are so positive.

00:01:13.673 --> 00:01:15.490
- I am. Yeah. I think I'm wired this way.

00:01:15.490 --> 00:01:18.270
Yeah. And then the house burned down.

00:01:18.270 --> 00:01:19.770
Again that was 15 years ago.

00:01:19.770 --> 00:01:22.290
And then last year a man high on drugs

00:01:22.290 --> 00:01:24.688
broke into our home while we were home.

00:01:24.688 --> 00:01:27.030
My teenage daughters up- were gone.

00:01:27.030 --> 00:01:30.090
He went up the stairs into
their rooms, took everything.

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:31.620
My son was playing video games.

00:01:31.620 --> 00:01:33.030
My husband and I were-

00:01:33.030 --> 00:01:35.448
had the bedroom door closed
so the cat wouldn't get in

00:01:35.448 --> 00:01:39.450
and he robbed us blind,
drove off in our car

00:01:39.450 --> 00:01:42.450
including stole my
Haagen-Dazs ice cream bars.

00:01:42.450 --> 00:01:43.283
He had a sweet tooth.

00:01:43.283 --> 00:01:44.250
- [Kelly] What?

00:01:44.250 --> 00:01:46.260
- Those are expensive;
there's only three in a pack.

00:01:46.260 --> 00:01:47.460
You know the ones I'm talking about.

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:48.600
Do you know what I mean?

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:50.640
And, but the best part
about the rose color

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:51.870
is my daughter Hayes said to me

00:01:51.870 --> 00:01:53.730
Oh my gosh, mom, we're so cursed.

00:01:53.730 --> 00:01:54.563
This is my middle daughter.

00:01:54.563 --> 00:01:56.820
She's like, the house burned
down and now this guy broke in.

00:01:56.820 --> 00:01:58.530
And I said, no, we are blessed.

00:01:58.530 --> 00:02:00.000
We were not home during the fire

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:02.520
and we never saw the man that broke in.

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:04.080
We found... They found
him living out of our car

00:02:04.080 --> 00:02:05.250
but we never saw him.

00:02:05.250 --> 00:02:06.240
So it was like the best one-

00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:07.800
- [Kelly] How big is that house?

00:02:07.800 --> 00:02:09.930
- Not big. My dad was visiting.

00:02:09.930 --> 00:02:11.880
My 88 year old dad slept
through the whole thing.

00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:12.810
He's like, Everybody good?

00:02:12.810 --> 00:02:13.749
And he went back to bed.

00:02:13.749 --> 00:02:15.120
I was like
- This is like a show!

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:17.040
- I know. Who does this happen to?

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:18.990
- Like I wouldn't believe this script.

00:02:18.990 --> 00:02:21.360
- No. And they found him
from the DNA from one

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:23.328
of the Haagen-Dazs bars that he dropped.

00:02:23.328 --> 00:02:26.400
- [Constance] No. No, that's too perfect.

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:30.090
- But I mean, I just
think life you put on-

00:02:30.090 --> 00:02:32.520
I just tend to sort of
say, okay, we are blessed.

00:02:32.520 --> 00:02:34.230
Like it could have been so much worse.

00:02:34.230 --> 00:02:35.063
- [Constance] Nobody was hurt?

00:02:35.063 --> 00:02:36.310
= Nobody was hurt. And we didn't-

00:02:36.310 --> 00:02:39.977
- Also, nobody looks at that
as a positive situation Kit.

00:02:39.977 --> 00:02:40.810
No one.

00:02:40.810 --> 00:02:43.187
I'm like really positive
and I don't know that I-

00:02:43.187 --> 00:02:44.349
- [Kit] It was a tough one

00:02:44.349 --> 00:02:45.900
- But it's a blessing.

00:02:45.900 --> 00:02:46.950
- Yes, I know.

00:02:46.950 --> 00:02:48.330
I'm kind of annoying that way.

00:02:48.330 --> 00:02:50.040
So I was thinking my
memoir would have to be

00:02:50.040 --> 00:02:52.320
like rose colored glasses or something.

00:02:52.320 --> 00:02:55.410
Yeah. Even this, you know,
I got this job at age 40.

00:02:55.410 --> 00:02:58.650
Yeah. I'm now 52 and I feel
like having to hit my stride.

00:02:58.650 --> 00:03:00.660
So I was was like, that's
another positive thing.

00:03:00.660 --> 00:03:01.493
- No, that is good.

00:03:01.493 --> 00:03:03.930
Your book would be very
interesting as well.

00:03:03.930 --> 00:03:06.480
Well Kit, we've gotta
talk about your shows. So-

00:03:06.480 --> 00:03:07.500
I said plural shows.

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:08.333
- Thank you. Thank you.

00:03:08.333 --> 00:03:10.079
- What's new on Access this season?

00:03:10.079 --> 00:03:12.178
- My name is in the title, ladies.

00:03:12.178 --> 00:03:14.239
(woman makes horn noise)

00:03:14.239 --> 00:03:16.350
There it is. You know what that means?

00:03:16.350 --> 00:03:18.330
13 years I've been there

00:03:18.330 --> 00:03:20.700
and now I can show up
without my badge, right?

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:22.050
And I told them I love it so much

00:03:22.050 --> 00:03:23.160
I'm gonna show up regardless,

00:03:23.160 --> 00:03:24.630
but that just secures me maybe

00:03:24.630 --> 00:03:25.860
for a little bit longer.

00:03:25.860 --> 00:03:26.760
Having a ball.

00:03:26.760 --> 00:03:27.593
- But that's amazing.

00:03:27.593 --> 00:03:29.130
My face is literally

00:03:29.130 --> 00:03:31.765
on this building and I
still have to show my badge

00:03:31.765 --> 00:03:33.510
(women laugh)

00:03:33.510 --> 00:03:36.090
- But it looks different coming in, Kit

00:03:36.090 --> 00:03:38.757
- So, they're probably
like, "No you're not."

